  "notes": "\"The fast end of the lane\", and the research ties two parameters directly to that tempo: hats on 16ths, which it calls out as \"denser than the genre norm to match the tempo\", and extra 16th-note kick pickups. So this is the only entry in the batch whose hat base is 16th outright, with `kick.densityPerBar` up at 4–6 and `syncopation` at 0.55 — both the highest here — while the tempo band tops out at 110. The melodic content moves the other way: \"frequently a repeated 3-note figure rather than a chord loop\", so `densityPerBar` stays low and `contour.riff` is 0.7. The bass is a syncopated 16th riff with short decay rather than a sustain, which is `independent_riff` with high anticipation and a small glide. Crash and reverse-cymbal transitions are the `percs` lanes; the mid-verse double-time switches are why `arrangement.transitions.switchUpProb` is 0.45, the highest here. ⚠ The `chromatic` scale entry is authored from the research's \"minor and chromatic\" and carries a low weight — it is a colour on a minority of seeds, not the model's centre. ⚠ `medium` because the research rates it medium-high and says the tempo range is catalog-level. The inferred parameters are the swing amount and the crash density. ⚠ The bass ceiling came down from 46 to 45 so it stays under a chord part that starts at 46 — `coherence.rs` requires the highest bass note to sit at or below the lowest chord note, and this model overlapped by 1.",
